green-agents-explained

This product includes concepts, terms, and file references from open work by
the Green Software Foundation (https://github.com/Green-Software-Foundation).

1. Reference implementations
   Source: https://github.com/Green-Software-Foundation/reference-implementations
   Commit 122780ca36b07a9a53d5a1a5f63514157958f1d9 (2 September 2026)
   Mainly: tools/gsf/agentic-ai-impact-explorer and
   specifications/sci-for-ai/gsf/llm-inference
   License: MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Green Software Foundation.
   No code is copied. The full MIT License text is in the LICENSE file of the source.

2. SCI for AI specification
   Source: https://sci-for-ai.greensoftware.foundation/ and
   https://github.com/Green-Software-Foundation/sci-ai
   Commit e8d3534f72b26e7b114c9054050db60f4543bb60 (7 September 2026)
   The specification materials are "Copyright (c) 2021 Joint Development Foundation
   Projects, LLC, GSF Series and its contributors. All rights reserved."
   This guide only describes the specification in new words and links to it.
   It does not copy specification text.

3. Green Software Patterns
   Source: https://github.com/Green-Software-Foundation/patterns
   Commit 36ccf754849bce89af87fb5222f7bce069cd2ffd (10 September 2026)
   License: CC BY 4.0 (Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International).
   License text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
   The reduction levers adapt ideas (new words, not copied text) from these patterns,
   all submitted by Navveen Balani (https://github.com/navveenb):
   - Use right-sized and energy-efficient AI models
     (docs/development/right-sized-energy-efficient-ai-models.md)
   - Optimize agent orchestration to reduce unnecessary model calls
     (docs/development/optimize-agent-orchestration-reduce-model-calls.md)
   - Use on-demand execution for AI and agent workloads
     (docs/architecture/system-topology/on-demand-execution-ai-agent-workloads.md)
   - Use carbon-aware scheduling and region selection for AI workloads
     (docs/operations/carbon-aware-ai-scheduling.md)
   Changes: the ideas are summarized in Simplified Technical English and combined
   into one list of levers.

This repository is an independent guide. It is not an official part of the
Green Software Foundation, and the Foundation did not review it.

Changes from the sources:
- The main concepts are written again in Simplified Technical English.
- The three diagrams in assets/ are new.
- SKILL.md is a new agent skill (Agent Skills format) that helps one person
  estimate the footprint of one agent.
- No code, figures, or specification text are copied.

Language
--------
The text is in Simplified Technical English (ASD-STE100).
- Idea to ask an AI model to write in ASD-STE100: Andrej Karpathy (https://github.com/karpathy),
  post on X: https://x.com/karpathy/status/2105819303471976479
- Text and checks: the simplified-technical-english agent skill by pili
  (https://github.com/0xpili), https://github.com/0xpili/simplified-technical-english
- ASD-STE100 is a specification and registered trade mark of ASD (AeroSpace and Defence
  Industries Association of Europe). This repository is not related to ASD.
